<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef generally weak on light to moderate demand and offerings.  Select and Choice chuck and round cuts steady to weak, while loin cuts weak and rib cuts uneven. Beef trimmings generally steady on fairly good demand and moderate to heavy offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>275 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>107 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>44 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     100.97	100.56	 95.85	 94.73</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.67	 -0.75	 -0.24	 -0.59</p>
<p>Rib	  161.66	160.90	156.48	156.56</p>
<p>Chuck	 65.77	 64.49	 66.98	 63.87</p>
<p>Round	 82.80	 82.80	 80.63	 80.63</p>
<p>Loin	 167.10	167.35	146.61	145.59</p>
<p>Brisket     59.25	 59.25	 59.07	 59.07</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  65.01	 64.93	 65.24	 65.08</p>
<p>Flank	 58.49	 58.49	 56.08	 56.08</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
